This is a classic DataTables issue 👍
Your table is rendering, but DataTables JS is NOT initializing, which is why:

❌ No search box
❌ No pagination
❌ Looks like a normal HTML table

Let’s fix it step-by-step, starting from the most common causes.


---

✅ 1️⃣ CHECK: jQuery MUST load BEFORE DataTables

DataTables depends on jQuery.
If jQuery loads after DataTables → nothing works (no error, just silent failure).

✅ CORRECT ORDER (VERY IMPORTANT)

Put this ONCE, preferably in _Layout.cshtml, before </body>:

<script src="https://code.jquery.com/jquery-3.7.1.min.js"></script>

<link rel="stylesheet"
      href="https://cdn.datatables.net/1.13.6/css/jquery.dataTables.min.css" />

<script src="https://cdn.datatables.net/1.13.6/js/jquery.dataTables.min.js"></script>

❌ Do NOT load jQuery again inside the page.


---

✅ 2️⃣ CHECK: Table ID MUST MATCH EXACTLY

HTML

<table id="itemsTable" class="table table-bordered table-striped">

JavaScript

$('#itemsTable').DataTable();

❌ These will NOT work:

$('#itemTable')   // missing "s"
$('#ItemsTable') // case mismatch

IDs are case-sensitive.


---

✅ 3️⃣ CHECK: DataTable INIT MUST RUN AFTER TABLE EXISTS

✅ SAFE VERSION (USE THIS)

<script>
    $(document).ready(function () {
        if ($('#itemsTable').length) {
            $('#itemsTable').DataTable({
                pageLength: 5,
                searching: true,
                ordering: true,
                lengthChange: false
            });
        }
    });
</script>

If the table is inside:

@if (ViewBag.StudentList != null)

then DataTables will not initialize when list is empty.

✔ The if ($('#itemsTable').length) check fixes this.


---

✅ 4️⃣ CHECK: Table MUST HAVE <thead> and <tbody>

DataTables requires <thead>.

✅ CORRECT

<table id="itemsTable" class="table">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th>Control No</th>
            <th>Serial No</th>
            <th>Model</th>
            <th>Category</th>
            <th>Location</th>
            <th>Qty</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        @foreach (var item in list)
        {
            <tr>
                <td>@item.ControlNo</td>
                <td>@item.SerialNo</td>
                <td>@item.Name</td>
                <td>@item.CategoryName</td>
                <td>@item.LocationName</td>
                <td>@item.Quantity</td>
            </tr>
        }
    </tbody>
</table>

❌ Missing <thead> = DataTables won’t activate.


---

✅ 5️⃣ CHECK: Are There JavaScript Errors?

Open Browser DevTools → Console.

Common errors:

jQuery is not defined

$(...).DataTable is not a function


🔥 Meaning:

Error	Cause

jQuery is not defined	jQuery not loaded
DataTable is not a function	DataTables loaded before jQuery OR duplicate jQuery
No error but no UI	Init ran before table existed



---

✅ 6️⃣ DO NOT LOAD SCRIPTS MULTIPLE TIMES

❌ This breaks DataTables:

<script src="jquery.js"></script>
<script src="jquery.js"></script> <!-- DUPLICATE -->

✔ Only ONE jQuery version allowed.


---

✅ 7️⃣ QUICK TEST (COPY–PASTE)

Paste this temporarily under your table:

<script>
    console.log("jQuery:", typeof $);
    console.log("DataTable:", typeof $.fn.DataTable);
</script>

Expected output:

jQuery: function
DataTable: function

If DataTable: undefined → library not loaded.


